#: ../../source/caseless_README.md:1
msgid ""
"Caseless -- wrap an object to set and get property with caseless "
"semantics but also preserve caseing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/caseless_README.md:3
msgid ""
"This library is incredibly useful when working with HTTP headers. It "
"allows you to get/set/check for headers in a caseless manner while also "
"preserving the caseing of headers the first time they are set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/caseless_README.md:5
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/caseless_README.md:15
msgid "has(key)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/caseless_README.md:17
msgid ""
"Has takes a name and if it finds a matching header will return that "
"header name with the preserved caseing it was set with."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/caseless_README.md:23
msgid "set(key, value[, clobber=true])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/caseless_README.md:25
msgid ""
"Set is fairly straight forward except that if the header exists and "
"clobber is disabled it will add `','+value` to the existing header."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/caseless_README.md:33
msgid "swap(key)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/caseless_README.md:35
msgid "Swaps the casing of a header with the new one that is passed in."
msgstr ""

